From a22b97e57b74f4809886ff0593eb3b7872c10ae1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 05:29:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Harden offload copy verification and source protection

- Verify each replica from disk: fsync (F_FULLFSYNC on macOS) the partial
  file, then re-read it with the page cache bypassed (F_NOCACHE /
  POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED) before comparing SHA-256 with the source.
- Compare the checksum before publishing: a mismatching copy is deleted
  instead of being renamed to the final clip name, so a corrupt replica
  never sits at a real clip path and a retry is not blocked as a collision.
- fsync the destination directory after the rename.
- Refuse plans whose replica project folder overlaps a source folder, so
  nothing is ever written onto the camera card.
- Fail a file as source_changed when the source size/mtime changes between
  scan, hashing and copy completion.
- Record source read errors as a failed file (source_read_failed) instead
  of raising out of the offload without persisting results.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
